Package: os7-module
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: important
Depends: os7-powershell (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Recommends: zfsutils-linux
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: The OS/7 and Zfs PowerShell modules
 OS/7's own command surface: the release identity, storage, boot environments,
 rollback, backup, home directories and the classic desktop, as PowerShell
 cmdlets — and the generic ZFS layer they run on.
 .
 TWO MODULES, and the direction between them is the point. Zfs knows nothing
 about OS/7 and would run on any OpenZFS host; OS7 is the product layer above
 it and reaches ZFS only through it. They travel in one package because that
 rule is only true if both are present — an OS7 module on a machine without Zfs
 is a module that cannot do anything.
 .
 zfsutils-linux is a Recommends and not a Depends on purpose: the modules load,
 report and self-test on a machine with no pools, which is what makes them
 checkable during an image build and on a rescue system.
